&lt;li&gt;Shape product experiences that feel native to enterprise contexts, collaborating cross-functionally to ensure terminology, flows, and interactions land with sophisticated buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in content design, UX writing, or content strategy, with at least 3 years focused on B2B or enterprise products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine curiosity about AI and how it changes your craft. You use Claude (or other LLMs) in your actual work as a thinking partner. You have opinions about what outputs are good enough, where it falls short, and how to bridge that gap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with code. You don&#39;t need to be an engineer, but you can read a codebase, ship small changes, and collaborate fluently with developers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong prototyping instincts and fluency in Figma. You think in interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing content for complex technical products and sophisticated buyers—fintech, dev tools, healthcare, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of enterprise buying journeys and the ability to craft content that works for end users, practitioners, and executives simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Portfolio that shows strategic thinking, clear writing for technical audiences, and content that moved business metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building from scratch. You&#39;ve created content systems, not just inherited them. You&#39;re energized by ambiguity, not paralyzed by it&lt;/li&gt;
