&lt;li&gt;Build and continuously refine the AWM sales methodology by incorporating learnings into playbooks and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of enterprise sales experience in Asset &amp;amp; Wealth Management technology, preferably driving adoption of SaaS or emerging technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of sales leadership experience, ideally 3+ leading teams within the Enterprise segment focused on AWM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building and leading high-performing sales teams selling into asset managers, wealth managers, private banks, and family offices, with demonstrated success in coaching and developing AEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing and scaling sales processes, tools, and methodologies in fast-growing organizations serving AWM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical acumen and ability to understand complex AI solutions and their applications in portfolio management, research, and client advisory, with experience enabling teams to have credible technical conversations with AWM stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of successful partnership with technical teams throughout the customer journey within financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of AWM buying cycles, procurement frameworks, and key pain points across hedge funds, asset managers, wealth managers, and private banks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to navigate complex, multithreaded sales cycles across diverse stakeholder groups and drive cross-functional initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex enterprise sales cycles within financial institutions and helping AEs secure strategic deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational rigor in pipeline management, forecasting, and sales metrics specific to AWM sales cycles&lt;/li&gt;
