&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in operating systems security or kernel development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of Linux internals, including kernel subsystems and security frameworks (SELinux, AppArmor, seccomp, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with kernel hardening techniques and exploit mitigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming skills in C and systems programming languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with eBPF for security monitoring and enforcement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of virtualization and containerization security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of identifying and fixing OS-level security vulnerabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with security-focused Linux distributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Strong candidates may also have:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kernel development experience or contributions to Linux kernel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real-time or embedded operating systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of hardware security features and their OS integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with secure boot technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with confidential computing and memory encryption technologies (SEV, TDX, SGX)&lt;/li&gt;
